---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import ShareRow from '../../components/ShareRow.astro';
import ArticleEndCTA from '../../components/ArticleEndCTA.astro';
import { SITE_URL, ORG_ID, PERSON_ID, SLUGS } from '../../lib/site';

const path = SLUGS.whoAmIWithoutTitle;
const title = 'Who Am I Without My Title? Identity After the Role';
const description =
  'Who am I without my title? When identity fuses with your role, stepping back can feel like disappearing. Here is how to build a self bigger than the job.';

const canonical = new URL(path, SITE_URL).href;

// Article + FAQPage — schema types preserved from the design, enriched with
// entity @ids so the founder/org graph resolves.
const schema = [
  {
    '@type': 'Article',
    '@id': `${canonical}#article`,
    headline: 'Who Am I Without My Title? Identity After the Role',
    author: { '@id': PERSON_ID },
    publisher: { '@id': ORG_ID },
    about: ['who am i without my title', 'identity after career', 'enmeshment with work'],
    description:
      'Why leaders fuse identity with their role, why letting go feels like disappearing, and how to build a self larger than the job.',
    mainEntityOfPage: `${canonical}#webpage`,
  },
  {
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: [
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Why do I feel like I am nothing without my job?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: "Because over years of high performance, your identity quietly fused with your role — a pattern sometimes called enmeshment or role identity fusion. The title became the main source of your worth, purpose and belonging, so imagining life without it feels like disappearing. It's extremely common in successful leaders and it's changeable: you can build a sense of self that includes the role without being consumed by it." } },
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'How do I separate my identity from my career?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: "Start by noticing where 'what I do' has replaced 'who I am,' then deliberately rebuild the parts of you the job crowded out — relationships, values, the body, meaning beyond output. Small, consistent reps of showing up as a person rather than a position gradually widen your identity so it no longer stands or falls with the title." } },
    ],
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={path}
  ogType="article"
  ogTitle="Who Am I Without My Title? Identity After the Role"
  ogDescription="When the role becomes the self, losing it feels like vanishing. It doesn't have to."
  bodyBg="#EFE8DA"
  schema={schema}
>
  <SiteHeader
    audience="leaders"
    variant="slim"
    logoHref={SLUGS.leaders}
    contextLink={{ label: 'The Legendary Leader →', href: SLUGS.legendaryLeader }}
  />

  <div style="background:#EFE8DA;color:#1B1810;">
    <article>
      <header style="max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:52px 32px 0;">
        <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="font-size:13px;color:#8A7F6C;margin-bottom:22px;display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;">
          <a href={SLUGS.leaders} style="color:inherit;text-decoration:none;">For Leaders</a><span>/</span><span style="color:#C04A26;">Who Am I Without My Title</span>
        </nav>
        <h1 style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(34px,5vw,54px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-0.02em;color:#1B1810;max-width:18ch;">Who am I without my title?</h1>
        <div style="margin-top:28px;background:#F4F0E7;border-left:3px solid #C04A26;border-radius:0 12px 12px 0;padding:24px 26px;">
          <p style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8A7F6C;margin-bottom:10px;">The short answer</p>
          <p class="bl-speakable" style="font-size:18px;line-height:1.6;color:#2E2A22;">If the thought of losing your role feels like disappearing, it's because your identity quietly <em style="font-style:italic;">fused</em> with it. The title became your main source of worth and belonging. That's incredibly common in strong leaders — and it can change. You can build a self that <em style="font-style:italic;">includes</em> the role without being consumed by it.</p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <section style="max-width:820px;margin:44px auto 0;padding:0 32px;">
        <div style="font-size:19px;line-height:1.72;color:#2E2A22;">
          <p style="margin-bottom:22px;">It creeps up over years. Early on the role is something you <em style="font-style:italic;">do.</em> Then the wins stack, the responsibility grows, the identity narrows — and somewhere along the way "what I do" quietly became "who I am." Now retirement, a sale, a step back, even a slow week can trigger a low-grade dread you'd never say out loud: <em style="font-style:italic;">if I'm not this, what am I?</em></p>
          <p style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-style:italic;font-size:24px;line-height:1.4;color:#1B1810;margin:34px 0;padding-left:22px;border-left:3px solid #C04A26;">A title is something you hold. It was never meant to be the whole of who you are.</p>
          <p>The fix isn't to care less about your work — it's to become <em style="font-style:italic;">bigger</em> than it. To rebuild the parts of you the role crowded out: relationships, values, the body, meaning beyond output. Done in small, consistent reps, your identity widens until it no longer stands or falls with a job title. The role becomes one strong thing you do — not the fragile whole of you.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section style="max-width:820px;margin:52px auto 0;padding:0 32px;">
        <div style="background:#15130E;color:#F4F0E7;border-radius:18px;padding:40px 42px;text-align:center;">
          <p style="font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#E0744A;margin-bottom:14px;">Start widening the self — free</p>
          <h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(26px,3.4vw,36px);line-height:1.1;color:#FBF8F1;max-width:24ch;margin:0 auto 16px;">Meet the person underneath the position.</h2>
          <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:rgba(244,240,231,0.78);max-width:48ch;margin:0 auto 28px;">The free Mindset Workouts train exactly this — seeing what's running you and rebuilding a self that's bigger than the role. Ten minutes is enough to start.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:14px;align-items:center;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;">
            <a href={SLUGS.workouts} style="background:#C04A26;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;padding:16px 28px;border-radius:10px;font-weight:700;font-size:16px;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;">Try a Mindset Workout — free <span>&rarr;</span></a>
            <a href={SLUGS.legendsJourney} style="border:1px solid rgba(244,240,231,0.3);color:#F4F0E7;text-decoration:none;padding:16px 26px;border-radius:10px;font-weight:600;font-size:15.5px;">Find where you are</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section style="max-width:820px;margin:56px auto 0;padding:0 32px 90px;">
        <h2 style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(24px,3vw,32px);line-height:1.1;color:#1B1810;margin-bottom:28px;">Straight answers</h2>
        <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px;">
          <div><h3 style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-weight:500;font-size:20px;color:#1B1810;margin-bottom:8px;">Why do I feel like nothing without my job?</h3><p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.65;color:#56524A;">Because your identity fused with your role over years of high performance — the title became your main source of worth, purpose and belonging. It's very common in successful leaders, and it's changeable: you can build a self that holds the role without being consumed by it.</p></div>
          <div><h3 style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-weight:500;font-size:20px;color:#1B1810;margin-bottom:8px;">How do I prepare for retirement or an exit emotionally?</h3><p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.65;color:#56524A;">Start before the date. Rebuild the parts of your identity the role crowded out — relationships, meaning, the body — so that when the title goes, the person doesn't. The leaders who transition well began widening their sense of self while still in the seat.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>
      <!-- internal-linking: keep-reading rail -->
      <section style="max-width:860px;margin:8px auto 0;padding:0 32px 76px;">
        <p style="font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:0.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#C04A26;margin-bottom:16px;">Keep reading</p>
        <div style="display:grid;gap:12px;">
          <a href="/leaders/successful-but-unfulfilled/" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;text-decoration:none;background:#F4F0E7;border:1px solid rgba(27,24,16,0.12);border-radius:12px;padding:18px 22px;">
            <span style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-size:19px;color:#1B1810;line-height:1.25;">Successful but unfulfilled — when the win feels empty</span>
            <span style="color:#C04A26;font-weight:700;font-size:16px;">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/leaders/whats-next-after-success/" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;text-decoration:none;background:#F4F0E7;border:1px solid rgba(27,24,16,0.12);border-radius:12px;padding:18px 22px;">
            <span style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-size:19px;color:#1B1810;line-height:1.25;">What's next after you've already made it</span>
            <span style="color:#C04A26;font-weight:700;font-size:16px;">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/leaders/leadership-plateau/" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;text-decoration:none;background:#F4F0E7;border:1px solid rgba(27,24,16,0.12);border-radius:12px;padding:18px 22px;">
            <span style="font-family:'Newsreader',serif;font-size:19px;color:#1B1810;line-height:1.25;">Why growth stalls: the leadership plateau</span>
            <span style="color:#C04A26;font-weight:700;font-size:16px;">&rarr;</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
      <ArticleEndCTA maxWidth={820} />
      <ShareRow title={title} maxWidth={820} />
</article>
  </div>

  <SiteFooter audience="leaders" variant="slim" />
</BaseLayout>
